= Political Rally

Mass rallies are an effective way to whip up enthusiasm in support of the revolution. What should our message to the crowd be?

- @united_front: Rally in support of the United Front
- @nationalism: Rally against imperialist oppression
- @democracy: Rally for legal and constitutional governance
- @welfare: Rally for economic reform and prosperity for all
- @local: A mixture of various local and national concerns that resonate most with the audience.
- @easy_discard

@united_front
on-arrival: ccp_dual_members_strength += 5

We rally alongside Communist cadres, stirring up the crowd with a show of revolutionary unity and the promise of societal change and equalization. The middle and bourgeois classes look on with suspicion, however.

@nationalism
on-arrival: west_relation -= 1

We stage a rally protesting imperialist domination of the country. Foreign citizens living in nearby concessions watch nervously.

@democracy
on-arrival: center_strength += 5

We rally on promises of constitionalism and democratization. While the people are broadly supportive, this stance is somewhat complicated by the fact of our status as a one-party state.

@welfare
on-arrival: left_strength += 5

The poverty of the masses is unbearable, and our promises to revitalize the economy and uplift the people are met with eager ears.

@local
on-arrival: center_strength += 5

Our organizers on the ground feel out the mood of the audience and respond to the most prevalent issues of the local area.


